div-mod-pow2 — machine-checked invariant (Tier 1)

  /opt/Isabelle2025-2/bin/isabelle build -D . Invariant

STATUS: checked. Isabelle2025-2, log written to
~/.isabelle/Isabelle2025-2/heaps/*/log/Invariant.{db,gz}. Built from
scratch (`-c`) with `quick_and_dirty = false`, so no `sorry`/`oops` can be
hiding in it. Runtime ~30 s (HOL image already present; ~6 min on a cold
image).

What is proved in Invariant.thy:

  div_mod_pow2_sound    non_negative e ==> 0 <= eval e
      The verdict the transform publishes never has a false positive: every
      node it marks SHIFTABLE has a genuinely non-negative dividend, so
      rewriting `/ 2^n` to `>> n` cannot turn -3/2 = -1 into -3>>1 = -2.

  pow2_pos              pow2 (Num n) ==> n > 0 & (EX k. n = 2 ^ k)
      A marked divisor is a real power of two — the exact divisor the shift
      rewrite needs.

  non_negative_bin_iff  non_negative (Bin op l r) <-> (op = "+" | op = "*")
                          & non_negative l & non_negative r
      The one-step unfolding: the analysis does not miss a "+"/"*" node
      whose operands it proved (a false negative the manifest allows does
      not happen for this easy case).

  shift_agrees          (0 <= n; d = 2 ^ k) ==> n div d = n div 2 ^ k
      The semantic content of the consumers, not just of the verdict.

Because the transform is analysis-only (it mutates nothing and returns
false), this semantic lemma IS its whole obligation — there is no
program-transformation step to justify.

NEGATIVE CONTROL (observed, not assumed): adding

  lemma "non_negative (Bin ''-'' (Num 0) (Num 5))" by simp

makes the build FAIL with `goal (1 subgoal): 1. False`. A green session is
therefore not vacuous.

Scope: Tier 1 — arithmetic only, no shell semantics, pure HOL, no AFP.
It says nothing about bash word splitting, `IFS`, or `${v:0}` on arrays.
Those need the semantics layer this file deliberately does not attempt.
